WEBVTT

00:00:02.430 --> 00:00:08.029
<v Tomasz Nowak>Morning, everyone. Tuesday the twentieth. Can you hear me? Teams has picked the wrong microphone again.</v>

00:00:09.490 --> 00:00:16.839
<v Priya Raman>Yeah, you're there. Bit tinny. More importantly, there's a birthday cake in the office. Actual cake, not those sad cereal bars.</v>

00:00:18.929 --> 00:00:26.280
<v Jamie Brennan>Lovely. I'm already thinking about weekend plans and the weather's looking rubbish. Walking boots or just the pub, that's the decision.</v>

00:00:27.530 --> 00:00:31.379
<v Fiona Doyle>It's Tuesday, mate. Ambitious bit of forward planning, even for me.</v>

00:00:32.810 --> 00:00:36.310
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, before this becomes the social committee. Finished stuff first?</v>

00:00:38.590 --> 00:00:45.939
<v Sarah Okafor>Yeah so, tested the GT1 Compressor Section yesterday and it's all fine now. That's done, not carrying anything over on it.</v>

00:00:48.000 --> 00:00:49.399
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good, closed off then.</v>

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:56.600
<v Sarah Okafor>And I already swapped the filter on the pick and place on two yesterday. That one's finished as well.</v>

00:00:57.630 --> 00:01:05.680
<v Grace Liu>Same from me on the water booster. Already swapped the filter on the water booster yesterday, so that's not another job for today.</v>

00:01:08.129 --> 00:01:11.980
<v Aisha Begum>Nice to have a couple actually off the list for once.</v>

00:01:13.349 --> 00:01:23.150
<v Grace Liu>Only an observation: noticed the Line 1 Mould Temperature Controller was running a bit warm on nights but it settled down. Nothing I'm putting forward as new work.</v>

00:01:24.819 --> 00:01:26.569
<v Tomasz Nowak>Understood. Settled down, observation only.</v>

00:01:28.379 --> 00:01:35.379
<v Fiona Doyle>And I heard a slight rattle from the turbine one compressor, nothing to action yet. Just mentioning what I heard.</v>

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:41.480
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yep, not turning that into a job on the strength of a passing noise.</v>

00:01:41.819 --> 00:01:49.870
<v Priya Raman>Oh, and the shutdown on the Fire Alarm Panel is cancelled now, production need it running. Take that out of the conversation entirely.</v>

00:01:50.189 --> 00:01:52.640
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right, cancelled. Nobody's working to that shutdown.</v>

00:01:54.209 --> 00:02:01.560
<v Aisha Begum>I'm still waiting on parts for the line three, nothing we can do until they arrive. Still blocked, same as yesterday.</v>

00:02:03.989 --> 00:02:08.889
<v Jamie Brennan>Yeah, no parts here to change that position. Not claiming we've magically unblocked it.</v>

00:02:10.909 --> 00:02:14.409
<v Tomasz Nowak>Okay, that stays blocked. Onto what we can actually agree.</v>

00:02:15.650 --> 00:02:22.650
<v Tomasz Nowak>I'll investigate the pressure drop on the GT2 inlet valve. Top priority please, that one — I'm taking it myself.</v>

00:02:24.879 --> 00:02:30.129
<v Priya Raman>Right, Tomasz has the pressure-drop investigation. No assuming the cause before you've had a look.</v>

00:02:30.530 --> 00:02:35.430
<v Aisha Begum>Sorry, just coming over you — that's separate from the seal replacement, isn't it?</v>

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:43.729
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, separate. I'll replace the seals on the GT2 Inlet Water Injection Valve as well. That's normal priority.</v>

00:02:44.909 --> 00:02:49.810
<v Fiona Doyle>Got it, Tom. Seal replacement at normal priority, not bundled into the top-priority investigation.</v>

00:02:52.240 --> 00:02:56.789
<v Tomasz Nowak>Exactly. Two distinct bits of work; don't merge them because both say GT2.</v>

00:02:59.229 --> 00:03:06.580
<v Tomasz Nowak>Fiona Doyle, can you recalibrate the sensors on the line 3 chiller today at 2pm? It matters but it's not urgent.</v>

00:03:08.710 --> 00:03:13.960
<v Fiona Doyle>Yeah, I'll recalibrate the sensors on the line 3 chiller today at 2pm. That's fine.</v>

00:03:16.020 --> 00:03:21.270
<v Aisha Begum>At two, rather than finished before two? Just so we're all hearing the same thing.</v>

00:03:21.840 --> 00:03:28.490
<v Fiona Doyle>At two, yeah. It matters but it's not urgent — no need to turn it into a panic job.</v>

00:03:29.719 --> 00:03:31.819
<v Tomasz Nowak>Spot on. That's the timing agreed.</v>

00:03:32.389 --> 00:03:41.490
<v Sarah Okafor>On the outfeed conveyor, the supplier still hasn't confirmed the delivery. That's still a blocker on the delivery side, not a new chase I'm adding here.</v>

00:03:42.939 --> 00:03:46.789
<v Jamie Brennan>Correct. Delivery's unconfirmed; nothing new to report from stores on that.</v>

00:03:48.810 --> 00:03:56.860
<v Sarah Okafor>But the existing kit, separate thing: I'll clear the jam and check the sensors on the outfeed conveyor at half two. Normal priority.</v>

00:03:59.120 --> 00:04:04.370
<v Tomasz Nowak>Thanks, Saz. You're taking the jam and sensor check, not promising anything about that delivery?</v>

00:04:05.469 --> 00:04:10.370
<v Sarah Okafor>Exactly. I can do that work on what's there. Doesn't unblock the supplier delivery.</v>

00:04:12.819 --> 00:04:14.919
<v Grace Liu>Right, two separate issues. That's clearer.</v>

00:04:16.490 --> 00:04:23.139
<v Tomasz Nowak>And I'll chase the purchase order for the guard switch on two by next Tuesday. Normal priority on that.</v>

00:04:23.819 --> 00:04:26.620
<v Jamie Brennan>Cheers, Tomasz. You've got the purchase-order chase, then.</v>

00:04:27.220 --> 00:04:31.769
<v Tomasz Nowak>Yeah, the chase only. I'm not slipping a fitting job into that sentence.</v>

00:04:33.670 --> 00:04:36.819
<v Fiona Doyle>Next Tuesday for that one, understood. Not this afternoon.</v>

00:04:37.470 --> 00:04:43.069
<v Priya Raman>I'll do the lock-out tag-out sign-off on the 11kV Switchboard by end of day. It's urgent.</v>

00:04:44.850 --> 00:04:48.350
<v Tomasz Nowak>Thanks, PR. Urgent sign-off, by end of day, with you.</v>

00:04:50.420 --> 00:04:54.620
<v Priya Raman>Yep. Specifically the lock-out tag-out sign-off, not an instruction to energise anything.</v>

00:04:54.990 --> 00:04:56.389
<v Grace Liu>Understood. Important distinction, that.</v>

00:04:57.910 --> 00:05:02.810
<v Tomasz Nowak>Grace, can you schedule downtime for the GT1 fuel valve with production? Low priority.</v>

00:05:04.480 --> 00:05:10.079
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, I'll schedule downtime for the GT1 fuel valve with production. Low priority, I've got it.</v>

00:05:12.339 --> 00:05:16.189
<v Sarah Okafor>Just the scheduling agreement, yeah? Not saying we're stopping it now.</v>

00:05:17.360 --> 00:05:21.910
<v Grace Liu>Yeah, agreeing the downtime with production. Not calling a stop in this meeting.</v>

00:05:23.170 --> 00:05:30.170
<v Tomasz Nowak>Jamie, can you do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet by the end of the week? Top priority please.</v>

00:05:31.670 --> 00:05:39.019
<v Jamie Brennan>Yep, I'll do the pre-use checks on the Forklift Fleet by the end of the week. Taking that as top priority.</v>

00:05:41.509 --> 00:05:47.459
<v Grace Liu>And just to be clear, pre-use still means before use. The end-of-week deadline isn't a free pass.</v>

00:05:49.180 --> 00:05:53.029
<v Jamie Brennan>Absolutely. Not treating the deadline as permission to use anything unchecked.</v>

00:05:54.430 --> 00:05:56.180
<v Tomasz Nowak>Good, we're aligned on that.</v>

00:05:57.170 --> 00:06:04.519
<v Tomasz Nowak>Grace, can you sort the permit to work and isolation for the AC1 by the 28th? Drop everything for that one.</v>

00:06:05.540 --> 00:06:13.240
<v Grace Liu>Yes, I'll sort the permit to work and isolation for the AC1 by the 28th. Understood — drop everything for that one.</v>

00:06:14.480 --> 00:06:20.079
<v Fiona Doyle>Sorry, Grace, just checking the order against the GT1 fuel valve scheduling. That stays low priority?</v>

00:06:20.970 --> 00:06:26.920
<v Grace Liu>It does. The AC1 permit and isolation takes precedence; the GT1 fuel valve scheduling stays low priority.</v>

00:06:28.779 --> 00:06:31.930
<v Tomasz Nowak>Right. That's deliberate, not two things both secretly first.</v>

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:40.649
<v Aisha Begum>And my blocked line three parts aren't being confused with the line 3 chiller calibration? Similar names, different conversation.</v>

00:06:41.930 --> 00:06:47.180
<v Fiona Doyle>No confusion here. My line 3 chiller calibration is agreed; your parts-dependent work stays blocked.</v>

00:06:49.459 --> 00:06:55.410
<v Sarah Okafor>All clear from me. Outfeed conveyor jam and sensors at half two, normal priority. Delivery still separate.</v>

00:06:56.920 --> 00:07:02.519
<v Priya Raman>Lovely. We done? I can see someone through the office window making very unequal cake slices.</v>

00:07:03.779 --> 00:07:09.379
<v Jamie Brennan>That's why I don't trust office catering. Weather's miserable and now the cake allocation's gone wrong.</v>

00:07:10.029 --> 00:07:17.029
<v Tomasz Nowak>You'll survive. Thanks, everyone — agreed work as discussed, finished stuff stays closed and the cancelled shutdown stays cancelled. Cheers.</v>
